message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "EviCon: evidence contracts for safe continuation after ambiguous remote effects (research prototype)"
type: software
version: "084"
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: "Nguyen"
    given-names: "Tran Thanh Lam"
    email: "lamntt@hcmute.edu.vn"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Information Technology, HCMC University of Technology and Engineering, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam"
repository-code: "https://github.com/lamnguyentt92/evicon"
keywords:
  - Internet of Things
  - remote effects
  - idempotency
  - evidence contracts
  - fault injection
  - preregistration
abstract: >-
  EviCon models the evidence a remote effect owner (a device, a broker plus device, a cloud API) offers
  after a client's command becomes ambiguous (dedup, receipt query, per-identity stop, certified fence,
  atomic receipt, owner expiry), measures that evidence black-box under injected faults (EviCon-Probe),
  and uses only measured evidence in a runtime that admits commands against a cumulative bound. The
  release contains the Go runtime and simulator, the probe, a Zephyr firmware, a TLA+ model, the
  preregistrations of every confirmatory experiment with their results, and the reviewer driver that
  reproduces the testbed runs and the paper's tables.
